"C:\\Program Files\\PowerShell\\7\\pwsh.exe" -NoProfile -Command "@'
# T-004 — M0, M1, M2 complete

2026-10-17. Director integrated two bounded Luna workers (Notes and Shell services). Only src/AntiQuickPad/ and the two authorized T-004 report/status files were written. No git operations, network, spike edits, or shared STATUS.md edits. Manager owns commits.

## Built

- M0: Program/App/MainWindow separation; Shell, Notes, Editor, Carousel folders; one default Look record for palette, interface/editor fonts, size and gutter; RuntimePaths. Opaque themed window, AvaloniaEdit styling. The integrated GUI selftest opened and focused this window.
- M1: One borderless, topmost resident window/editor; hide/show retains both. Esc hides; tray Show / Hide and Quit; tray click shows/focuses. SID/logon-scoped mutex/event enforces one resident process; second launch signals show, including requests received during startup. Ctrl+Alt+Shift+A registration uses Avalonia's Win32 hook and MOD_NOREPEAT. Default is defined in GlobalHotkey.DefaultGesture; override through ANTIQUICKPAD_HOTKEY (e.g. Ctrl+Alt+F8). Registration outcome/errors are logged and unavailable status appears in the tray tooltip. Reopen briefly accents the window border without delaying focus.
- M2: NotesSession exposes note list, CurrentIndex, Current, CreateNote, DeleteCurrent, Select, UpdateCurrent and Save. MainWindow exposes CreateNote, DeleteCurrentNote and SelectNote; Ctrl+N creates a note. No carousel UI yet. GUID-named plain .md files plus notes.json for order/current index/caret. Same-directory temporary files are renamed over destinations; manifest is written after content. Autosave debounces text/caret changes by 350 ms; hide/quit flush synchronously. Save errors retain the open window and show a status message. Corrupt manifests/missing content fail loading rather than silently replacing notes.

Normal data: %LOCALAPPDATA%/AntiQuickPad/notes/. Log: %LOCALAPPDATA%/AntiQuickPad/logs/shell.log. Selftest uses a unique bin/Release/net10.0/selftest/<id>/ directory, bypasses the production singleton and hotkey/tray, and never touches real notes. Its isolated singleton check uses separate names. Test artifacts are retained in ignored build output for inspection.

## Verification

From src/AntiQuickPad/ (PowerShell):

"'```powershell
$env:AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT = '"'1'
dotnet build -c Release --no-restore
dotnet bin/Release/net10.0/AntiQuickPad.dll --selftest
"'```

Final build: **exit 0, 0 warnings, 0 errors**. Telemetry opt-out is needed here: without it the cached Avalonia build task tries to write its logger outside the sandbox. No package/config changes or network were needed.

Final selftest: **exit 0**. Checks actual Avalonia startup focus; three internal toggle hide/show cycles; same editor reference; visible/focused state; real debounce persistence; next-process text/current-index/caret reload; create/select/delete and deleting the final note; isolated second-process singleton signal delivered into the resident show/focus path.

Final internal show-to-editor-focus samples: **5.344 ms, 2.048 ms, 30.390 ms**, each <100 ms. Earlier integration samples were 3.580 / 2.964 / 2.798 ms. These are bounded scripted Release samples, not a physical-hotkey latency distribution or compositor-paint measurement. The production WM_HOTKEY callback captures Stopwatch ticks at message arrival and passes them through the same show path; completion is logged when Avalonia reports editor keyboard focus.

Final evidence log: src/AntiQuickPad/bin/Release/net10.0/selftest/e9b4cc05c8214bbbb41ad613d113241c/logs/shell.log.

## Unverified / follow-up

- User must verify physical Ctrl+Alt+Shift+A delivery (close old spike copies if the chord is occupied), typing after reopen from another app, Esc, tray click/menu and Quit. Selftest deliberately avoids registering the real chord or installing a tray icon.
- Production launch using the normal LocalAppData location, foreground activation from unrelated apps, Windows session shutdown, and visual feel of the reopen cue require a normal desktop check. The process singleton transport and show path were checked automatically with an isolated name; a second normal application launch remains a useful manual check.
- Per-file replacement is atomic; the whole set of Markdown files plus manifest is not a transactional snapshot or backup system. Crash recovery and external-file conflict handling are outside M0–M2.
- No manual desktop control or inspection was performed. Carousel/Markdown decoration/settings UI remain later milestones.

Blockers: **none for T-004**. Ready for manager review/commit and physical shell checks.
